    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter June 1st with a condensed lineup, prioritizing high-floor production against a slate of difficult opposing arms. **Christian Yelich** stands out as today\u2019s clear primary play with a 62.48 score; despite facing a 3.72 xERA starter, his leadoff spot and a strong +13% dynamic platoon advantage leverage his high-contact profile, making him our most reliable asset for Runs and AVG. **Carson Benge** (51.46) also warrants a start in the UTIL slot; while his base projection is modest, the +10% boost from batting at the top of the order against Hancock makes him a significantly more efficient play than our bench depth. **Junior Caminero** (50.28) remains a locked-in start, though his matchup against Madden is concerning given the elite 2.31 xERA he faces, necessitating a reliance on his power floor despite the -19% SP skill penalty.\n\nOur bench decisions were dictated by a rigid adherence to the 40.0 efficiency floor, specifically intended to protect our game cap usage during a series of unfavorable pitching matchups. **Chase Meidroth** (39.23) was the closest to a start, but the -19% SP skill impact against Ryan ultimately pushed him just below the threshold. We are opting to bench **Dillon Dingler** (35.74) as well; despite a strong .373 xwOBA, the combination of a -15% dynamic platoon hit and a mid-range SP match makes him a clear liability today. The remaining bench, including **Casey Schmitt** and **Jacob Gonzalez**, failed to clear the floor primarily due to SP skill penalties exceeding 19%, confirming our strategy to sit them in favor of protecting our season-long aggregate caps for more advantageous environments. \n\nRisk management remains a priority given the SP landscape. While **Luke Raley** and **Colt Keith** occupy the middle infield spots with scores of 43.76 and 45.51 respectively, both are facing sub-3.60 xERA starters, which suppresses their ceiling. We are keeping a close watch on **Luke Raley** specifically, as his -10% SP skill penalty is compounded by park factors, leaving little margin for error if he doesn't secure an extra-base hit. With the scarcity of SB in this league, the absence of **Trea Turner** and **Caleb Durbin** from the active board today is noted, forcing us to rely on **Christian Yelich** and **Carson Benge** to manufacture offense at the top of the lineup.",
